WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.307
- I love this cat.

00:00:01.307 --> 00:00:02.708
I'm going to give her a hug.

00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:04.347
(cat purring)

00:00:04.347 --> 00:00:07.180
(Christmas music)

00:00:08.024 --> 00:00:09.315
- It's finally Christmas season.

00:00:09.315 --> 00:00:11.687
When I was younger, I
would always run and grab

00:00:11.687 --> 00:00:14.524
the toys catalogs and I would
just go through every page

00:00:14.524 --> 00:00:16.614
and circle every single toy that I wanted

00:00:16.614 --> 00:00:17.808
for Christmas that year.

00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:20.527
So, today what I'm gonna do
is I'm going to go and review

00:00:20.527 --> 00:00:23.348
the top selling toys from Target.

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:26.399
I have two of my friends
coming by to help me out

00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:28.869
'cause I really needed some
expert advice on this one.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:31.208
- I'm a toy expert.

00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:33.596
(laughing)

00:00:33.596 --> 00:00:34.966
(upbeat music)

00:00:34.966 --> 00:00:36.827
- I'm DJ, I'm a toy expert

00:00:36.827 --> 00:00:39.854
and no one knows more
about toys than I do.

00:00:39.854 --> 00:00:42.437
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.371 --> 00:00:45.166
- What's your favorite toy right now?

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:46.127
- What do I like...

00:00:46.127 --> 00:00:46.960
- My spy gear.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.863
- Your spy gear?

00:00:48.863 --> 00:00:49.958
- Fidget spinner.

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:52.721
- We're going to check
out what's in those.

00:00:52.721 --> 00:00:53.692
- Presents!

00:00:53.692 --> 00:00:55.758
- You can tell me what you like about it,

00:00:55.758 --> 00:00:56.812
if you think it's silly,

00:00:56.812 --> 00:00:58.393
if you think it's cool, alright?

00:00:58.393 --> 00:01:00.271
- What about if it's a toy I don't like?

00:01:00.271 --> 00:01:01.217
- You say that too.

00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:02.062
You want us to open that one?

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.123
- I do want to open it!

00:01:04.123 --> 00:01:06.756
- Alright, let's see what's inside.

00:01:06.756 --> 00:01:07.755
- Elmo!

00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:11.255
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:12.344 --> 00:01:15.011
(Elmo speaking)

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.825
- Whoa! He's funny.

00:01:19.362 --> 00:01:21.112
His belly is shaking.

00:01:24.261 --> 00:01:26.215
- This how you open toys on Christmas day?

00:01:26.215 --> 00:01:27.048
You're like-

00:01:27.048 --> 00:01:29.328
(paper ripping)

00:01:29.328 --> 00:01:31.661
Go ahead, this is your show.

00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:36.719
(Christmas music)

00:01:39.476 --> 00:01:40.882
(laughter)

00:01:40.882 --> 00:01:42.321
Tell me what that face was.

00:01:42.321 --> 00:01:45.477
- I know some kids love this
toy but I don't know why.

00:01:45.477 --> 00:01:47.216
I'll gift wrap it and give it to them

00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:48.795
for their birthday if they want.

00:01:48.795 --> 00:01:50.845
- If your dad got you Elmo for Christmas

00:01:50.845 --> 00:01:52.899
and this was under the tree,
how happy would you be?

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:55.585
I got my Elmo, I got
my Elmo, I got my Elmo.

00:01:55.585 --> 00:01:56.523
- I'm not liking it.

00:01:56.523 --> 00:01:57.596
- You really like Elmo?

00:01:57.596 --> 00:01:58.515
- Yes!

00:01:58.515 --> 00:02:02.279
I play with Elmo, wake up, take a nap,

00:02:02.279 --> 00:02:05.500
play with Elmo some more and eat my candy.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.190
- I don't care to like, wait
to get my stuffed animals

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.115
I want my stuffed animals right away.

00:02:10.115 --> 00:02:14.201
So, I gotta like, rub the
egg and all that stuff

00:02:14.201 --> 00:02:15.772
in order to get my stuffed animals?

00:02:15.772 --> 00:02:16.796
- What is this?

00:02:16.796 --> 00:02:17.922
- What is this?

00:02:17.922 --> 00:02:19.539
(laughter)

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.725
Yeah, we're good on this.

00:02:20.725 --> 00:02:21.872
I'm a put this on the side

00:02:21.872 --> 00:02:23.469
and we're gonna see
what else is over there.

00:02:23.469 --> 00:02:24.486
- Okay.

00:02:24.486 --> 00:02:25.319
A cat!

00:02:26.382 --> 00:02:30.527
(upbeat electronic music)

00:02:30.527 --> 00:02:31.746
Cut it out!

00:02:31.746 --> 00:02:33.304
- I'll cut it for you, alright?

00:02:33.304 --> 00:02:34.969
This is where that
editor puts that graphic

00:02:34.969 --> 00:02:36.077
five years later.

00:02:36.077 --> 00:02:38.577
(piano music)

00:02:40.432 --> 00:02:42.432
Whew! We finally did it.

00:02:43.631 --> 00:02:46.274
- I got you some milk, meow.

00:02:46.274 --> 00:02:49.290
He talks! He just say my name.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.038
I love this cat, I'm
going to give her a hug.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:52.960
(cat purring)

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.863
He likes to eat milk

00:02:54.863 --> 00:02:56.531
Mmm, so good.

00:02:56.531 --> 00:02:59.195
- Go ahead, rip it apart like
it's Christmas morning, man.

00:02:59.195 --> 00:03:02.043
(bell ringing)

00:03:02.043 --> 00:03:04.287
(futuristic music)

00:03:04.287 --> 00:03:05.620
- We're loaded.

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:10.504
- Oh, now we look like, boom boom!

00:03:10.504 --> 00:03:12.437
Did it, did it get ya?

00:03:12.437 --> 00:03:14.252
How do you, you can't even tell.

00:03:14.252 --> 00:03:16.666
How do you know who
wins, does it keep score?

00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:17.872
(beeping)

00:03:17.872 --> 00:03:18.990
That beep.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.158
(beeping)

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:20.991
Let's turn off this thing.

00:03:20.991 --> 00:03:21.824
- Yes.

00:03:21.824 --> 00:03:23.481
- Is this a toy that you would
recommend for your friends?

00:03:23.481 --> 00:03:25.400
- I like the toy but I hate the noise

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.056
and if you want to hide, I mean,

00:03:27.056 --> 00:03:29.896
you can at least turn
the toy off for a second.

00:03:29.896 --> 00:03:32.729
(Christmas music)

00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:36.083
- How would you score Elmo?

00:03:37.221 --> 00:03:39.530
You give him a five if you
really, really love him,

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.142
or you give him a one if you
only like him a little bit.

00:03:43.142 --> 00:03:43.975
- Five.

00:03:43.975 --> 00:03:44.808
- A five?

00:03:44.808 --> 00:03:47.599
- The one that I really
like better was the Laser X.

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:48.908
- And what about the kitten?

00:03:48.908 --> 00:03:49.846
- A five.

00:03:49.846 --> 00:03:51.179
- Five out of five?

00:03:51.179 --> 00:03:53.133
- This shouldn't be the
top selling toy at Target,

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.547
you don't do anything with it.

00:03:54.547 --> 00:03:55.936
- You love both of those toys?

00:03:55.936 --> 00:03:57.217
- Yes.

00:03:57.217 --> 00:03:59.527
- You can only get the Elmo or the cat,

00:03:59.527 --> 00:04:00.587
which one would you get?

00:04:00.587 --> 00:04:01.420
- Cat.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.534
- Are you hoping for any of these gifts

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:03.938
under your tree this Christmas?

00:04:03.938 --> 00:04:05.000
- That one.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.032
- I like the cat's fur, and
my kitten is my favorite toy.

00:04:09.032 --> 00:04:10.806
- You can bring a Laser X home

00:04:10.806 --> 00:04:14.763
and play whenever you want, whatever time.

00:04:14.763 --> 00:04:15.870
- The best, man.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.092
- Merry Christmas!

00:04:17.092 --> 00:04:19.435
- Happy holidays, peace.

00:04:19.435 --> 00:04:22.268
(Christmas music)

